<p>Elon Musk testified Tuesday in federal court in Oakland, California, at the start of a civil trial against OpenAI, Chief Executive Sam Altman, President Greg Brockman and Microsoft over whether the ChatGPT maker violated commitments tied to its founding as a nonprofit AI lab. Musk is seeking $150 billion in damages, with proceeds intended for OpenAI’s charitable arm, and wants OpenAI returned to nonprofit status and Altman and Brockman removed from leadership roles. Musk told the court the case was about charitable giving and said OpenAI had been created to develop artificial intelligence for the benefit of humanity rather than private profit. OpenAI lawyer William Savitt told jurors that Musk had supported a for-profit structure when he could control it, wanted “the keys to the kingdom,” and sued only after leaving OpenAI and later creating rival AI company xAI. The trial is expected to last about three weeks before U.S. District Judge Yvonne Gonzalez Rogers, who also warned Musk and Altman to limit social media commentary about the case.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/UVFoiu-Ib5zd-8kVEN0DlFt8tKff3N3pCjAlEHYTcZ2aCAk0zZQhvUSpYkVm-OWfBrJkOfhBxa3erioGcE8kQ8vVum2m04wSobLMDQRZOM9-YXnyp0ygioNzPi82bEgaPTRhLHYdwakp_IE3lWq7swBcnDxLHBAD8lJAqOJzFXUFnB2cne8Yf1E78iIuQZI02hM4PseV2iaeN1iQbI9ywitOaPw9bKjiFpyIvM9XAXhN3wZ1uXc3biOGPrL4wXJs4fumwgvR9YF1Yj1i6A' alt='Elon Musk arrives at the U.S. District Court in Oakland on Tuesday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Microsoft’s role: Its lawyer said Microsoft was not a behind-the-scenes co-conspirator and did not help OpenAI violate a charitable trust, portraying the company as a responsible partner that supplied resources.</li><li>Founding dispute: Musk said he conceived the idea, named OpenAI, recruited key people and provided initial funding; his lawyers put his early contribution at about $38 million in some accounts.</li><li>AI risk: Musk testified that he helped create OpenAI partly to counter Google’s AI efforts and warned of a possible “Terminator outcome” if powerful AI developed without adequate safeguards.</li></ul><blockquote>If we make it OK to loot a charity, the entire foundation of charitable giving in America will be destroyed - Elon Musk</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Elon Musk: Musk said he was not opposed to a small for-profit subsidiary so long as “the tail didn’t wag the dog,” and said his objection was to the loss of nonprofit control rather than the use of commercial tools. (<a href='https://yro.slashdot.org/story/26/04/29/0311202/musk-testifies-openai-was-created-as-nonprofit-to-counter-google'>Slashdot</a>)</li><li>OpenAI and Sam Altman: OpenAI’s legal team said Musk never required OpenAI to remain entirely nonprofit and contended there was no binding promise barring the later corporate structure. (<a href='https://www.nbcbayarea.com/news/local/opening-arguments-elon-musk-openai-lawsuit-live-updates/4076182/'>NBC Bay Area</a>, <a href='https://www.birgun.net/haber/elon-musk-tan-openai-kurucularina-tepki-insanliga-fayda-saglama-misyonuna-ihanet-ettiler-709106'>BirGün</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/economy/2026/4/28/musk-testifies-at-openai-trial-its-not-ok-to-loot-a-charity'>Musk testifies at OpenAI trial it’s not OK to ‘loot a charity’</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ndtv.com/world-news/elon-musk-accuses-openai-of-looting-charity-making-unsafe-ai-11423040#publisher=newsstand'>Elon Musk Accuses OpenAI Of &#x27;Looting Charity&#x27;, Making &#x27;Unsafe AI&#x27;</a> - ndtv.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cz027nyz529o'>Musk says basis of charitable giving at stake in OpenAI lawsuit</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1995884/musk-lawyer-says-openai-stole-a-charity-as-trial-against-ai-firm-sam-altman-begins'>Musk lawyer says OpenAI ‘stole a charity’, as trial against AI firm, Sam Altman begins</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/e